 from "},{"code":"matching","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"matching_algorithm","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumBipartiteMatching()"},{"type":"text","text":" on a bipartite graph for O(m √n) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartite.min_edge_cover"},{"type":"text","text":". Minimum when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"matching"},{"type":"text","text":" is maximum; from any other matching it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still an edge cover (a vertex covered by an edge added earlier in the pass is skipped). nil"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when some vertex has no edge. O(n + m)."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"minimumEdgeCover(matching:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumEdgeCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"matching","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Matching","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule0A0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumVertexCover()":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same with every weight 1. On a graph without self-loops it lies within the ends of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"m